connectedCallback() is a lifecycle callback function that is triggered automatically when the element is attached to DOM.



3. Define the custom element class:
    + The `HelloWorld` class is the class of the custom element, which we'll use when registering the custom element. 
    + [`connectedCallback()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Web_Components/Using_custom_elements#Using_the_lifecycle_callbacks) is a lifecycle callback function that is triggered automatically when the element is attached to DOM. class HelloWorld extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback() {
    this.innerHTML = '<br/><br/><br/>Hello World!';
  }
}
customElements.define('hello-world', HelloWorld);

Register the custom element class with the customElements.define(name, class) method. In the Editor, enter the registered name as the tag name when adding the custom element to the site. Once registered, the custom element can be used on your site.

